%T A400107 1,6,7,9,2,9,3,7,9,4,2,8,8,7,4,0,1,5,1,4,7,8,9,9,2,8,2,8,2,4,4,0,8,9,
%U A400107 9,0,4,4,9,6,5,3,9,2,8,5,7,5,6,4,6,3,2,5,2,7,0,8,0,4,9,1,2,2,1,1,3
%N A400107 Decimal expansion of Sum_{m >= 0, m not a binary self number} 2^(-m).
%C A400107 Binary self numbers are A010061.
%C A400107 The binary expansion of the constant directly encodes the complement of A010061: the coefficient of 2^(-m) is 1 iff m is not a binary self number.
%C A400107 This constant is transcendental, since its square divided by 8 is the transcendental binary self-number density constant A242403.
%D A400107 Steven R. Finch, Mathematical Constants, Cambridge University Press, 2003, p. 179.
%D A400107 József Sándor and Borislav Crstici, Handbook of Number theory II, Kluwer Academic Publishers, 2004, Chapter 4, p. 384-386.
%H A400107 Max Alekseyev, <a href="/A400107/b400107.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100000</a>
%H A400107 M. A. Alekseyev and N. J. A. Sloane, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.14365">On Kaprekar's Junction Numbers</a>, Journal of Combinatorics and Number Theory 12:3 (2022), 115-155; arXiv:2112.14365 [math.NT], 2021-2022.
%H A400107 G. Troi and U. Zannier, <a href="http://www.bdim.eu/item?id=BUMI_1999_8_2B_2_397_0">Note on the density constant in the distribution of self-numbers - II</a>, Bollettino dell'Unione Matematica Italiana, Serie 8, Vol. 2-B, No. 2 (1999), pp. 397-399; <a href="https://eudml.org/doc/urn:eudml:doc:194654">alternative link</a>.
%H A400107 Umberto Zannier, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9939-1982-0647887-4">On the distribution of self-numbers</a>, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc., Vol. 85, No. 1 (1982), pp. 10-14.
%F A400107 Equals Sum_{n>=1} 2^(-A228082(n)) = 2 - Sum_{k >= 1} 2^(-A010061(k)) = sqrt(8*A242403), where A242403 denotes the corresponding constant.
%e A400107 1.421718000192395178651281692...
%Y A400107 Cf. A010061, A228082, A242403, A386568, A386569.
